    deepExplanation: "Example:\n\n```ts\nconst name: string = \"TypeScript\";\nconst version: number = 5;\nconsole.log(name, version);\n```\n\nProduction pattern:\n\n```ts\nconst count: number = 42;\n// const invalid: number = \"42\";\n// Error: Type 'string' is not assignable to type 'number'.\n```\n\nWhy it matters: Improves correctness before runtime. Makes APIs and component contracts explicit. Supports refactoring and large-team collaboration. Provides architectural documentation through types.",
    productionExample: "```ts\nconst count: number = 42;\n// const invalid: number = \"42\";\n// Error: Type 'string' is not assignable to type 'number'.\n```",
